On Friday 18 September 2009 20:04:20 Jorge Llambías wrote:
> That's a good one, but for the second or third level. I wouldn't test
> anything concerning fu'ivla for the first level.

Fourth level, since it's a type 4 fu'ivla. The types of brivla tested should 
be gismu in the first level, more gismu and lujvo in the second, more lujvo 
and types 1, 2, and 3 fu'ivla in the third, and type 4 fu'ivla and all 
preceding in the fourth. Maybe we could test how to form a type-4 in the 
fifth level, but that'll require a fill-in-the-blank question. E.g.:

lo tricu be la'o ly. Tilia .ly. goi ko'a cu se valsi zoi gy. linden .gy. fa'u 
zoi sy. tilo .sy. fa'u zoi ry. lipa .ry. lo glico ku fa'u lo spano ku fa'u lo 
rusko .i ma poi vomoi klesi fu'ivla cu mapti valsi ko'a lo lojbo

There are several acceptable answers, such as {lindeno}, {tilnipa}, {lintilo}, 
and {lindipa}.

